WEBVTT

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.469
Last time
on Star Trek: Voyager...

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.768
I'm Captain Braxton
of the Federation Timeship Aeon.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.433
I've come
from 29th century Earth.

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:10.340
Why are you firing at us?

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:12.607
Your vessel is responsible
for a disaster in my century...

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:13.976
a temporal explosion
that will destroy

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.311
all of Earth's solar system.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:17.976
I've come back in time
to prevent that occurrence.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.642
My mission is your destruction.

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:24.847
We seem to be caught in some
kind of graviton distortion.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.950
We're being pulled in, too.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.298
I find it hard to believe
a ship from the 29th century

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:38.497
could have landed on this beach
without being noticed.

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:40.233
That ship shouldn't be here.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:41.968
It belongs to another century.

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:43.703
We have to take it back.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.540
No one else knows
there's something up there.

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.136
We've got to tell somebody
about this.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.169
We've got to call NASA.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.943
She's a security risk.

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:52.816
Go to Griffith, get the data,
get rid of her.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:54.649
What the hell did you do
to my computer?

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:55.654
It is screwed up!

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.019
The hard drive is wiped.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.055
Get down!

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:03.795
Starling is using 29th-century
technology against us.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.491
We may not be able
to keep up with him.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.137
Yes.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:13.896
He's accessing
our main computer.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:14.907
Get us back into orbit

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.067
and I want
a full damage report from...

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.076
Captain Janeway...

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.975
You're from the 24th century?

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:22.413
And here all this time, I
thought you were from the 29th.

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:24.781
Looks like I have
the home-field advantage.

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.911
And now the conclusion.

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:33.548
Let me guess.

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:35.151
Someone broke
into the van last night

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:37.493
while I was sleeping,
tried to snatch the stereo.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.929
You bravely fought them off

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:41.593
and now you're
repairing the damage.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.499
That's exactly what happened.

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:44.935
My hero.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:52.972
What's it like?

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:55.003
Life as a spy, I mean.

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.446
Classified.

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:58.246
Oh, right.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:59.945
I forgot.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:02.284
But you said "secret agent"

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:03.755
and nobody says secret agent.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:04.916
And you do that a lot.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.926
You get things
not quite right...

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.855
like you don't belong here.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:11.557
Rain, you're fantasizing.

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:14.226
And you're insulting
my intelligence.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.929
Yesterday afternoon,
I picked up a UFO in orbit.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.165
Today, my life is
completely out of control,

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:22.106
so don't think
I'm too stupid to notice.

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:25.740
I apologize.

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:27.678
Accepted.

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:29.204
Would you also accept

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:31.149
that there are lives
at stake here?

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:33.084
The more you keep
asking me questions,

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:36.555
the more difficult you
make things... for everybody.

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.422
I'll try.

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.493
So...

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.467
why'd you become an astronomer?

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:51.832
My brother.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:54.305
Had a telescope...
a little refractor.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.401
You could barely see in the tree
house next door actually, but...

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.002
it was enough.

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:03.243
It was enough to see
the rings of Saturn.

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:05.342
I remember...
I remember I used

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:06.852
to think
that they looked like...

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:09.616
jewels from a pirate's treasure.

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:14.952
All I ever wanted since then
was to...

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:18.520
reach up and touch them.

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:20.465
Good morning.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.927
Agent Tuvok, what's up?

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.494
Breakfast is up.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.062
Have you made any progress?

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:28.334
I think so.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.842
Chili burritos,
footlong hot dogs

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:32.469
and Goliath gulps.

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:33.706
This is not a breakfast.

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.805
This is an afternoon
at Dodger Stadium.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.839
And that is a non sequitur.

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:38.976
Would you please hand me
a burrito?

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:42.350
Everything you guys do
is just a little bit off.

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:48.753
These things are kind of...

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.558
crude.

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:52.531
So much for sending
a locator signal.

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:54.590
There is another option.

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.929
The radio dish
at the observatory.

00:03:57.971 --> 00:03:59.632
We could use the same setup...

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:03.039
The same setup that I used
to send that message to your...

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:06.944
whatever it is up in orbit.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.278
We will require your assistance.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.612
No kidding.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.447
Well?

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.146
Not on an empty stomach.

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:14.433
Starling downloaded
nearly 20 percent

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:16.704
of our computer core
while we were trying to beam

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:18.233
the timeship
out of his building.

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:20.302
I'm replacing those programs
as quickly as I can,

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:23.213
but some of it
isn't retrievable.

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:24.944
Like the Doctor.

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:26.780
There's literally
nothing left of him.

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:27.945
He's just... gone.

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:30.751
Unfortunately, the Doctor is
only one of our problems.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:31.950
Our weapons are off-line.

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:33.457
Tuvok and Paris
are still missing

00:06:33.493 --> 00:06:34.858
somewhere in Los Angeles,

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:37.658
and we've confirmed
Captain Braxton's hypothesis.

00:06:37.697 --> 00:06:39.824
If Starling does attempt
a flight to the future,

00:06:39.866 --> 00:06:42.460
it will most likely
end in disaster.

00:06:42.502 --> 00:06:46.097
Captain, I've analyzed
Braxton's...

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:48.198
uh, schematic.

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:51.335
The temporal technology
is incredibly complex.

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:54.505
No matter how much a genius
this Starling might be,

00:06:54.547 --> 00:06:57.209
he is not a trained pilot
from the 29th century.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:58.979
Without the exact calibration,

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:01.077
that ship will rip
the time-space continuum apart.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.918
The instant he jumps
to the 29th century,

00:07:04.023 --> 00:07:06.082
there won't be a 29th century...

00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:07.114
not for Earth, anyway.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:08.923
The entire solar system
will be destroyed.

00:07:09.028 --> 00:07:10.620
I want that timeship.

00:07:10.663 --> 00:07:13.188
Long-range transporters
are still down.

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:14.756
We'd have to drop
out of orbit again.

00:07:14.801 --> 00:07:17.770
Captain, I strongly
recommend against that.

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:23.571
The more legitimate
news organizations

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:25.873
have apparently decided
that the Voyager image

00:07:25.912 --> 00:07:26.879
is fraudulent.

00:07:26.913 --> 00:07:28.938
However, I've also
been monitoring

00:07:29.048 --> 00:07:30.515
more official channels,

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.677
and the United States
military is taking things

00:07:32.718 --> 00:07:34.083
just a little more seriously.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:36.486
If we risk another pass
through the lower atmosphere,

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:38.922
there's a chance of getting
intercepted by the Air Force.

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.949
If we can't get to the ship...

00:07:40.993 --> 00:07:43.791
maybe we can get to the man.

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:44.854
Torres, I want you to...

00:07:44.897 --> 00:07:47.627
Captain Janeway,
I'm receiving a transmission

00:07:47.667 --> 00:07:49.498
from Lieutenant Tuvok,
audio only.

00:07:49.535 --> 00:07:51.696
Mr. Tuvok, report.

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:54.069
Lieutenant Paris and I are
at the Griffith Observatory

00:07:54.106 --> 00:07:55.437
in the Hollywood Hills.

00:07:55.475 --> 00:07:57.466
We have modified
the satellite dish transmitter

00:07:57.510 --> 00:07:58.807
to carry and receive

00:07:58.845 --> 00:08:00.676
Voyager communication
frequencies.

00:08:02.014 --> 00:08:03.914
I regret the bad connection.

00:08:03.983 --> 00:08:05.075
It's quite all right, Mr. Tuvok.

00:08:05.117 --> 00:08:06.084
What's happened?

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:08.018
We have become associated
with a young woman

00:08:08.054 --> 00:08:10.386
employed at the astronomical
laboratory.

00:08:10.423 --> 00:08:12.687
It was she who sent
the message to Voyager,

00:08:12.725 --> 00:08:14.920
but her lab is under the
supervision of an individual

00:08:14.994 --> 00:08:16.518
named Henry Starling.

00:08:16.562 --> 00:08:18.621
Oh, we've met Mr. Starling.

00:08:18.664 --> 00:08:20.757
He has the timeship,
and he's the one

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:23.928
who will cause the disaster
in the 29th century.

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:26.130
Then it would seem we must
find a way to stop him.

00:08:26.172 --> 00:08:27.935
Tell me about this young woman.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:29.405
Can we trust her?

00:08:29.442 --> 00:08:33.071
She and Lieutenant Paris
appear to be bonding

00:08:33.112 --> 00:08:35.103
on a cross-cultural level.

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:37.883
I would have to say yes.

00:08:39.084 --> 00:08:41.780
Ask if she'd be willing
to help us.

00:09:06.845 --> 00:09:08.472
How's it going?

00:09:08.513 --> 00:09:10.310
I find your interest
in my well-being

00:09:10.348 --> 00:09:12.248
to be less than genuine.

00:09:12.284 --> 00:09:14.752
Try to be
a little more grateful, Doc.

00:09:14.786 --> 00:09:16.913
The schematics I downloaded
from your ship

00:09:16.988 --> 00:09:20.685
indicated you were stuck
in the Sick Bay 24 hours a day.

00:09:22.861 --> 00:09:25.352
I recently suffered
a severe program loss

00:09:25.397 --> 00:09:28.298
and I'm still in the process
of retrieving my memory files,

00:09:28.333 --> 00:09:30.096
but apparently,
on a few occasions,

00:09:30.135 --> 00:09:32.695
I have been projected
into other locations.

00:09:32.737 --> 00:09:35.672
Undoubtedly, you are using
a similar procedure.

00:09:35.707 --> 00:09:38.335
My holographic simulator.

00:09:38.376 --> 00:09:41.345
We use it to test
our new microchip designs.

00:09:41.379 --> 00:09:44.871
I projected you through
the emitters in the office.

00:09:44.916 --> 00:09:48.374
Your program really isn't
very sophisticated.

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:49.944
That is a matter of opinion.

00:09:49.988 --> 00:09:52.752
Now, would you please return me
to my vessel?

00:09:52.791 --> 00:09:55.157
Can't do that. Not yet.

00:09:55.193 --> 00:09:57.252
I've a few questions
I want answered.

00:09:57.295 --> 00:09:59.855
If you have need
of medical expertise,

00:09:59.898 --> 00:10:02.059
I would refer you
to a more local physician.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:03.067
All Captain Janeway's

00:10:03.101 --> 00:10:06.468
talk about a disaster I caused
is just smoke.

00:10:06.504 --> 00:10:09.962
You came here
to steal my timeship.

00:10:10.008 --> 00:10:12.203
That is simply not the case.

00:10:12.243 --> 00:10:14.973
That timeship is
from the 29th century...

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:17.173
technology 500 years
more advanced

00:10:17.215 --> 00:10:18.546
than anything you've got.

00:10:18.583 --> 00:10:20.141
You'd love to get
your hands on it.

00:10:20.185 --> 00:10:22.983
You figured I'd be
an easy target... some backwards

00:10:23.088 --> 00:10:26.216
20th-century Neanderthal
who doesn't know what he's got,

00:10:26.257 --> 00:10:27.884
but you found out otherwise,
didn't you?

00:10:27.926 --> 00:10:31.987
A paranoid response indicative
of bipolar personality disorder.

00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:34.863
If my history is accurate,

00:10:34.899 --> 00:10:36.764
Southern California
in the late 20th century

00:10:36.801 --> 00:10:38.996
had no shortage
of psychotherapists...

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:41.231
competent and otherwise.

00:10:41.272 --> 00:10:43.001
I suggest you find one.

00:10:43.108 --> 00:10:44.439
Now...

00:10:46.177 --> 00:10:47.906
return me to Voyager.

00:10:47.946 --> 00:10:52.246
I've learned
your weapons are damaged,

00:10:52.283 --> 00:10:54.274
your ship's teleporter
is half-shot,

00:10:54.319 --> 00:10:57.152
but I didn't get
all the personnel files.

00:10:57.188 --> 00:10:59.816
I have to know my enemy.

00:10:59.858 --> 00:11:03.885
Give me Captain Janeway's
psychological profile.

00:11:03.928 --> 00:11:06.795
I'm a doctor, not a data base.

00:11:06.831 --> 00:11:08.560
I'd say you're
a little bit of both.

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:09.658
Start talking.

00:11:10.702 --> 00:11:13.262
Or suffer the consequences?

00:11:13.304 --> 00:11:14.931
Hardly.

00:11:14.973 --> 00:11:17.168
I'm a hologram.

00:11:17.208 --> 00:11:20.336
I experience neither pain...

00:11:20.378 --> 00:11:22.243
nor fear of death.

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:24.009
You have no means
of coercing me.

00:11:27.352 --> 00:11:28.910
Pain.

00:11:31.656 --> 00:11:33.783
It's an interesting sensation,
isn't it?

00:11:33.825 --> 00:11:35.656
I...

00:11:35.693 --> 00:11:36.819
I never realized...

00:11:36.861 --> 00:11:38.988
How unpleasant it could be?

00:11:42.867 --> 00:11:45.802
This is what burning feels like.

00:11:45.837 --> 00:11:46.997
For a human

00:11:47.072 --> 00:11:49.734
to experience what you're
going through right now,

00:11:49.774 --> 00:11:51.708
he'd have to be on fire.

00:11:57.215 --> 00:11:58.307
How?

00:11:58.349 --> 00:12:01.648
By reconfiguring
your tactile response sensors.

00:12:01.686 --> 00:12:03.779
Easy as proverbial pie.

00:12:11.629 --> 00:12:14.427
Feeling more cooperative?

00:12:19.237 --> 00:12:20.966
I'm in a meeting, Dave.

00:12:22.707 --> 00:12:23.969
Put her through.

00:12:24.075 --> 00:12:25.542
Mr. Starling.

00:12:25.577 --> 00:12:26.976
Oh, my God, I'm so scared.

00:12:27.045 --> 00:12:28.444
They're going to find me.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:29.811
I don't know what to do.

00:12:29.848 --> 00:12:31.179
Take it easy, Rain.

00:12:31.216 --> 00:12:32.478
Everything's okay.

00:12:32.517 --> 00:12:33.677
Everything's not okay.

00:12:33.718 --> 00:12:35.379
People are shooting at me.

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:36.546
They're going to find me.

00:12:36.588 --> 00:12:37.714
I don't know what to do.

00:12:37.755 --> 00:12:38.847
Yes, you do.

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:41.552
You're going to jump in a cab
and come to my office.

00:12:41.593 --> 00:12:42.685
You'll be safe here.

00:12:42.727 --> 00:12:44.422
No, they'll find me.

00:12:44.462 --> 00:12:45.429
Where are you?

00:12:45.463 --> 00:12:48.091
Metro Plaza... by the fountain.

00:12:48.133 --> 00:12:51.227
Please come get me.
Please.

00:12:51.269 --> 00:12:52.531
I'll send somebody.

00:12:52.570 --> 00:12:53.696
No!

00:12:53.738 --> 00:12:55.399
You.

00:12:56.808 --> 00:12:58.969
I'm really scared.

00:13:00.411 --> 00:13:02.003
I'll be right there.

00:13:05.517 --> 00:13:07.610
He bought it... sort of.

00:13:07.652 --> 00:13:09.119
What do you mean?

00:13:09.154 --> 00:13:10.121
I don't know.

00:13:10.155 --> 00:13:12.316
His voice sounded
a little suspicious.

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:16.520
Pack a lunch, Doc.

00:13:16.561 --> 00:13:18.085
We're going for a walk.

00:13:18.129 --> 00:13:20.256
In case you have forgotten,

00:13:20.298 --> 00:13:22.289
I can only appear
in a room equipped

00:13:22.333 --> 00:13:24.460
with a holographic
projection system.

00:13:24.502 --> 00:13:27.335
In short, I'm going nowhere.

00:14:31.603 --> 00:14:33.537
Interferometric dispersion
is on line.

00:14:33.571 --> 00:14:35.801
That should take care
of any radar detection.

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:39.833
And I've configured the shields
to disguise our visual profile.

00:14:39.877 --> 00:14:42.107
Unless somebody gets
right on top of us,

00:14:42.146 --> 00:14:44.944
we should look like
a small 20th-century aircraft.

00:14:44.983 --> 00:14:47.178
Transporters are on line.

00:14:47.218 --> 00:14:50.187
We should be within range
in about ten minutes.

00:14:51.923 --> 00:14:55.620
You can see
the entire Baja Peninsula.

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:58.561
I'd forgotten how beautiful
the view is from this altitude.

00:14:58.596 --> 00:15:00.621
I never thought
I'd see it again.

00:15:02.634 --> 00:15:04.898
You trained as a pilot
in North America, didn't you?

00:15:04.936 --> 00:15:07.336
That's right.
My first year at the Academy.

00:15:07.372 --> 00:15:09.533
Then I went to Venus
for a couple of months

00:15:09.574 --> 00:15:11.701
to learn how to handle
atmospheric storms,

00:15:11.743 --> 00:15:16.180
and then I dodged asteroids
for a semester in the belt.

00:15:16.214 --> 00:15:17.772
It sounds like you had
a lot more fun

00:15:17.815 --> 00:15:19.578
at the Academy than I did.

00:15:19.617 --> 00:15:22.586
I remember dodging
a few punches in the lab.

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:26.613
Only you, B'Elanna, could start
a brawl in Astro-theory 101.

00:15:27.725 --> 00:15:30.558
I guess I was just
a little more...

00:15:30.595 --> 00:15:33.564
enthusiastic in those days.

00:15:33.598 --> 00:15:35.259
I guess so.

00:15:37.535 --> 00:15:39.628
Chakotay...

00:15:39.671 --> 00:15:41.662
what if we're stuck here?

00:15:41.706 --> 00:15:43.105
What if we can't

00:15:43.141 --> 00:15:44.438
find a way back?

00:15:44.475 --> 00:15:47.308
There are still
a few isolated places

00:15:47.345 --> 00:15:48.778
left in this century.

00:15:48.813 --> 00:15:50.781
We'd have to keep low profiles.

00:15:50.815 --> 00:15:52.305
We'd have to get jobs.

00:15:53.518 --> 00:15:56.351
I've thought about pursuing
archaeology full-time.

00:15:56.387 --> 00:15:57.979
Maybe I could teach
at a university,

00:15:58.056 --> 00:16:00.820
or work on one of the important
digs in Central America.

00:16:00.858 --> 00:16:02.450
There were still a lot
of important discoveries

00:16:02.493 --> 00:16:03.755
to be made in this century.

00:16:03.795 --> 00:16:06.229
I could win a Nobel prize.

00:16:08.232 --> 00:16:09.529
So much for a low profile.

00:16:11.569 --> 00:16:13.127
What about you?

00:16:14.305 --> 00:16:18.139
"Highly qualified Klingon
seeks position as engineer."

00:16:19.644 --> 00:16:21.168
I'd hire you in a second.

00:16:22.213 --> 00:16:24.306
Let's start our descent.

00:16:26.317 --> 00:16:28.649
Approach course laid in.

00:16:28.686 --> 00:16:30.313
Full power to thrusters.

00:16:31.389 --> 00:16:33.152
Watch out for birds.

00:16:47.605 --> 00:16:48.936
Paris to Chakotay.

00:16:48.973 --> 00:16:50.099
Go ahead.

00:16:50.141 --> 00:16:52.302
Starling's arrived,
with the Doctor.

00:16:52.343 --> 00:16:55.073
What?
How is that possible?

00:16:55.113 --> 00:16:56.080
I don't know.

00:16:56.114 --> 00:16:57.081
Are you within range?

00:16:57.115 --> 00:16:58.377
Almost.

00:16:58.416 --> 00:17:00.551
Another two minutes.

00:17:01.618 --> 00:17:03.085
I don't know, Doc...

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.145
you were awfully quiet
on the ride over here.

00:17:05.188 --> 00:17:07.588
I'm not programmed
to make small talk.

00:17:07.624 --> 00:17:09.091
Maybe just a little bit anxious

00:17:09.126 --> 00:17:10.787
about being out
in the real world.

00:17:10.827 --> 00:17:13.660
It's just another environment
to me.

00:17:17.367 --> 00:17:19.267
Mind your manners, Doc.

00:17:21.438 --> 00:17:23.406
If your shipmates
start any trouble,

00:17:23.440 --> 00:17:24.771
you'll be holo-dust.

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:32.948
I've triangulated the position
of the van, Chakotay.

00:17:32.983 --> 00:17:34.951
Stand by for tricorder uplink.

00:17:34.985 --> 00:17:38.011
You'll be able to lock on
the moment Starling is inside.

00:17:40.724 --> 00:17:43.284
Mr. Starling,
I'm so glad you're here.

00:17:43.327 --> 00:17:44.954
Tell your new friends
to come out

00:17:45.028 --> 00:17:47.121
or their colleague
here is going to die.

00:17:47.164 --> 00:17:48.597
What are you talking about?

00:17:50.901 --> 00:17:52.425
Let's go.

00:17:52.469 --> 00:17:54.164
Oh, my van is this way.

00:17:54.204 --> 00:17:55.694
We're taking my car.

00:17:57.774 --> 00:18:00.072
Well... I left my stuff
in the van.

00:18:00.110 --> 00:18:02.670
I'll send somebody back for it.

00:18:04.581 --> 00:18:06.139
Is there a problem?

00:18:06.183 --> 00:18:07.172
Nope.

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:11.547
He's heading
in the wrong direction.

00:18:11.588 --> 00:18:12.919
They're not going to the van.

00:18:12.990 --> 00:18:14.651
Mr. Chakotay,
there is a problem.

00:18:24.067 --> 00:18:27.798
That... that's the guy
that tried to kill me.

00:18:27.838 --> 00:18:30.170
No, he was trying to rescue you.

00:18:31.541 --> 00:18:32.565
Where are we going?

00:18:32.609 --> 00:18:34.600
To my office.
You'll be safe there.

00:18:34.645 --> 00:18:36.078
Office, right.

00:18:44.821 --> 00:18:46.379
We're recalibrating
Starling's position.

00:18:46.423 --> 00:18:48.482
You're going to have to take him
out of his own car.

00:18:50.927 --> 00:18:52.758
There may not be enough time.

00:18:55.098 --> 00:18:56.360
I've determined the coordinates.

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:57.389
Now, Chakotay!

00:18:58.402 --> 00:18:59.960
We've got a lock
on Starling's position.

00:19:00.003 --> 00:19:01.231
Energizing.

00:19:01.271 --> 00:19:04.331
Dunbar, take
the surface streets.

00:19:04.374 --> 00:19:06.205
The 101's a nightmare
this time of...

00:19:06.243 --> 00:19:08.677
Oh, my God!

00:19:09.646 --> 00:19:10.510
Run!

00:19:14.451 --> 00:19:16.282
Pattern buffer's overloading.

00:19:16.319 --> 00:19:18.549
He's activated
some kind of device.

00:19:18.588 --> 00:19:21.489
It's interfering
with the transport.

00:19:31.601 --> 00:19:33.330
Hmm!

00:19:58.295 --> 00:19:59.421
Are you all right?

00:19:59.463 --> 00:20:00.521
I guess so.

00:20:00.564 --> 00:20:01.531
Doctor?

00:20:01.565 --> 00:20:03.965
I've been equipped
with an autonomous,

00:20:04.067 --> 00:20:06.592
self-sustaining,
mobile holo-emitter.

00:20:06.636 --> 00:20:10.197
In short, I am footloose
and fancy-free.

00:20:13.043 --> 00:20:15.341
Captain, we've got Starling
in our transporter buffers,

00:20:15.378 --> 00:20:17.403
but we can't rematerialize him.

00:20:17.447 --> 00:20:19.881
The interference is disrupting
computer pathways.

00:20:19.916 --> 00:20:21.611
Aft thrusters are down.

00:20:24.054 --> 00:20:25.453
Captain, we're close enough
to the shuttle

00:20:25.489 --> 00:20:26.683
to use the short-range
transporter.

00:20:26.723 --> 00:20:27.985
Janeway
to Transporter Room 1.

00:20:28.058 --> 00:20:29.753
Lock directly on
to the shuttle's pattern buffers

00:20:29.793 --> 00:20:30.760
and energize.

00:20:30.794 --> 00:20:31.818
Acknowledged.

00:20:31.862 --> 00:20:33.625
Chakotay, we're taking over
from here.

00:20:33.663 --> 00:20:35.130
Mr. Kim, let's go.

00:20:38.935 --> 00:20:40.334
The buffers are purged.

00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:42.736
They've taken Starling
off our hands.

00:20:42.773 --> 00:20:45.537
We're losing altitude.

00:20:51.748 --> 00:20:53.841
He's got what looks like
a tricorder.

00:20:56.286 --> 00:20:58.880
It's putting out some kind
of interference signal.

00:21:00.557 --> 00:21:03.458
I'm isolating it
and suppressing the amplitude.

00:21:06.563 --> 00:21:07.757
Got him.

00:21:10.333 --> 00:21:11.960
Damn it.

00:21:13.203 --> 00:21:14.465
Janeway to Sick Bay.

00:21:14.504 --> 00:21:16.472
Medical emergency
in Transporter Room 1.

00:21:16.506 --> 00:21:18.269
Acknowledged, Captain.

00:21:22.412 --> 00:21:23.845
Propulsion is off-line.

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:26.542
Voyager, we're going down.

00:22:32.549 --> 00:22:33.743
Where are we?

00:22:36.386 --> 00:22:37.751
This one looks like an Indian.

00:22:39.022 --> 00:22:40.455
And that one...

00:22:40.490 --> 00:22:42.424
I don't know what her story is.

00:22:45.896 --> 00:22:48.126
What's that thing on her head?

00:22:57.774 --> 00:22:59.298
Careful, Butch.

00:22:59.342 --> 00:23:02.038
She looks like a fighter.

00:23:02.078 --> 00:23:03.306
Who are you?

00:23:03.346 --> 00:23:04.711
You first.

00:23:04.748 --> 00:23:08.309
Are you spying on us... Chief?

00:23:11.821 --> 00:23:13.516
No.

00:23:13.556 --> 00:23:14.955
Just passing by.

00:23:15.025 --> 00:23:17.721
In your new stealth plane?

00:23:17.761 --> 00:23:19.422
Who sent you?

00:23:19.462 --> 00:23:21.828
Nobody sent us.

00:23:21.865 --> 00:23:24.732
We had engine trouble.

00:23:24.768 --> 00:23:26.326
I don't believe her.

00:23:26.369 --> 00:23:28.564
They're wearing
military uniforms,

00:23:28.605 --> 00:23:29.936
flying a secret plane.

00:23:29.973 --> 00:23:31.304
They're coming for us.

00:23:31.341 --> 00:23:34.469
"USS" equals federal government.

00:23:34.511 --> 00:23:37.708
The federal government
is the beast.

00:23:37.747 --> 00:23:40.511
We are not from the beast.

00:23:40.550 --> 00:23:42.450
Just take us to our plane.

00:23:42.485 --> 00:23:43.076
Shut up!

00:23:45.755 --> 00:23:47.154
That'll be all!

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:48.487
Call for reinforcements.

00:24:01.504 --> 00:24:03.768
It's going to be a long day.

00:24:10.814 --> 00:24:12.213
I've gone out with guys

00:24:12.248 --> 00:24:13.442
who've disappeared
into thin air

00:24:13.483 --> 00:24:14.541
on the first date.

00:24:14.584 --> 00:24:16.916
I assume she is speaking
figuratively.

00:24:16.953 --> 00:24:20.787
But I have never
actually seen it happen,

00:24:20.824 --> 00:24:22.689
and you, Mr. Leisure Suit...

00:24:22.726 --> 00:24:25.058
There's a name
I hadn't considered.

00:24:25.095 --> 00:24:27.962
That guy punched you
a bunch of times.

00:24:27.998 --> 00:24:32.958
You should have a black eye
or a swollen lip, a broken nose.

00:24:33.003 --> 00:24:34.129
Try to relax.

00:24:34.170 --> 00:24:37.333
You appear to be...
hallucinating.

00:24:37.374 --> 00:24:40.070
Oh, is that what I am?

00:24:40.110 --> 00:24:42.101
I'm hallucinating.

00:24:42.145 --> 00:24:44.136
Rain, I'm sorry you got
dragged into all this.

00:24:46.416 --> 00:24:48.407
Tuvok here.

00:24:48.451 --> 00:24:50.078
Tuvok, we've got Starling,

00:24:50.120 --> 00:24:52.486
but we've lost contact
with Chakotay and Torres.

00:24:52.522 --> 00:24:54.649
Their shuttle went down
over Arizona.

00:24:54.691 --> 00:24:56.420
Mr. Kim is transmitting
the coordinates

00:24:56.459 --> 00:24:57.927
to your tricorder.

00:24:58.060 --> 00:24:58.958
I want you to find them.

00:24:58.994 --> 00:25:01.189
Aye, Captain.
Tuvok out.

00:25:03.432 --> 00:25:05.423
Mr. Starling is under control.

00:25:06.769 --> 00:25:08.634
I suggest you return
to Chronowerx

00:25:08.671 --> 00:25:10.468
and continue the business there.

00:25:10.506 --> 00:25:13.703
The Doctor and I must
make our way to Arizona.

00:25:18.814 --> 00:25:20.213
He suffered
minor synaptic stress

00:25:20.249 --> 00:25:23.082
during the extended transport,
enough to cause unconsciousness,

00:25:23.118 --> 00:25:24.107
but not any permanent damage.

00:25:24.153 --> 00:25:25.643
Can you bring him out of it?

00:25:25.688 --> 00:25:27.212
Yes, Captain.

00:25:32.428 --> 00:25:35.488
Welcome to the 24th century.

00:25:36.598 --> 00:25:39.431
I took the precaution
of removing your tricorder.

00:25:39.468 --> 00:25:41.402
That's what it's called,
by the way.

00:25:41.437 --> 00:25:42.495
It didn't work.

00:25:42.538 --> 00:25:44.529
It should have blocked
your ship's teleporter.

00:25:44.573 --> 00:25:45.540
It works perfectly.

00:25:45.574 --> 00:25:47.064
You just don't know
how to use it.

00:25:47.109 --> 00:25:48.940
Give me some credit, Captain.

00:25:48.978 --> 00:25:51.173
I did pretty well
for a primitive.

00:25:51.213 --> 00:25:52.976
Well, that's all over now.

00:25:53.082 --> 00:25:54.344
I've won,

00:25:54.383 --> 00:25:56.943
so disable the force field
around Chronowerx.

00:25:56.986 --> 00:25:58.851
I want that timeship.

00:25:58.887 --> 00:26:01.720
You're in no position to be
making any demands, Captain.

00:26:01.757 --> 00:26:03.019
On the contrary.

00:26:03.058 --> 00:26:04.787
What are you going to do...
shoot me?

00:26:04.827 --> 00:26:06.920
The thought has crossed my mind.

00:26:06.962 --> 00:26:08.361
Well, it wouldn't
get you anything.

00:26:08.397 --> 00:26:10.126
I've rigged the timeship.

00:26:10.165 --> 00:26:12.861
If you try to teleport it again,
if you even go near it,

00:26:12.901 --> 00:26:15.665
Los Angeles will look like
the face of the moon.

00:26:15.704 --> 00:26:18.195
You'd destroy an entire city?

00:26:18.240 --> 00:26:20.538
You don't care about the future.

00:26:20.576 --> 00:26:21.838
You don't care
about the present.

00:26:21.877 --> 00:26:23.936
Does anything
matter to you, Mr. Starling?

00:26:23.979 --> 00:26:25.742
The betterment of mankind.

00:26:25.781 --> 00:26:27.043
It doesn't look like that.

00:26:27.082 --> 00:26:29.380
Why do you think I want
to go to the future?

00:26:29.418 --> 00:26:30.851
A vacation?

00:26:31.920 --> 00:26:34.684
To get more technology.

00:26:34.723 --> 00:26:37.191
That's why you're launching
the timeship.

00:26:37.226 --> 00:26:40.559
I've cannibalized the ship
itself as much as I can.

00:26:40.596 --> 00:26:44.054
There's nothing left to base
a commercial product on.

00:26:44.099 --> 00:26:47.535
And the future is just waiting
to be exploited.

00:26:47.569 --> 00:26:48.797
You just don't get it, do you?

00:26:48.837 --> 00:26:51.567
I created the microcomputer
revolution.

00:26:51.607 --> 00:26:54.371
Using technology
you never should have had.

00:26:54.410 --> 00:26:56.970
Irrelevant... my products
benefit the entire world.

00:26:57.012 --> 00:26:58.570
Without me, there would be

00:26:58.614 --> 00:27:00.980
no laptops, no Internet,
no bar code readers.

00:27:01.016 --> 00:27:02.244
What's good for Chronowerx

00:27:02.284 --> 00:27:04.411
is good for everybody.

00:27:04.453 --> 00:27:05.579
I can't stop now.

00:27:05.621 --> 00:27:07.418
One trip to the 29th century,

00:27:07.456 --> 00:27:09.321
and I can bring back
enough technology

00:27:09.358 --> 00:27:12.350
to start the next ten
computer revolutions.

00:27:12.394 --> 00:27:15.557
If you even attempt
to travel to the future,

00:27:15.597 --> 00:27:18.725
you'll risk creating
a temporal explosion

00:27:18.767 --> 00:27:21.361
that could cost
billions of lives,

00:27:21.403 --> 00:27:22.597
including your own.

00:27:22.638 --> 00:27:25.903
I'm willing to take that risk.

00:27:25.941 --> 00:27:27.932
In my time...

00:27:28.010 --> 00:27:30.342
Mr. Starling,

00:27:30.379 --> 00:27:33.940
no human being would dream
of endangering the future

00:27:34.049 --> 00:27:36.449
to gain advantage
in the present.

00:27:36.485 --> 00:27:38.453
Captain, the future
you're talking about...

00:27:38.487 --> 00:27:40.148
that's 900 years from now.

00:27:40.189 --> 00:27:42.453
I can't be concerned
about that right now.

00:27:42.491 --> 00:27:43.753
I have a company to run

00:27:43.792 --> 00:27:46.352
and a whole world full of people
waiting for me

00:27:46.395 --> 00:27:48.625
to make their lives
a little bit better.

00:27:52.801 --> 00:27:55.429
Computer,
reactivate force field.

00:27:59.575 --> 00:28:04.035
Chronowerx stock
is about to crash.

00:28:24.865 --> 00:28:29.768
There are two forces
at work in the world...

00:28:29.804 --> 00:28:31.101
the drive toward collectivity

00:28:31.138 --> 00:28:33.368
and the drive
toward individuality.

00:28:33.407 --> 00:28:36.205
You are the former
and I am the latter.

00:28:36.243 --> 00:28:37.938
We told you,

00:28:38.012 --> 00:28:40.446
we are not from the
United States government

00:28:40.481 --> 00:28:41.573
and we are not...

00:28:41.615 --> 00:28:44.778
The beast has many heads
and I'm looking at two of them.

00:28:44.819 --> 00:28:46.184
Listen, I used to think

00:28:46.220 --> 00:28:48.882
violence could be
the solution to a problem,

00:28:48.923 --> 00:28:49.947
but it's not true.

00:28:50.024 --> 00:28:51.958
You are no patriot.

00:28:52.026 --> 00:28:54.460
I was a freedom fighter...
so I thought.

00:28:54.495 --> 00:28:55.962
That gun will get you nowhere.

00:28:55.996 --> 00:28:57.293
Porter!

00:28:57.331 --> 00:28:59.629
They're coming... the Feds.

00:29:00.768 --> 00:29:02.133
How many?

00:29:02.169 --> 00:29:03.158
Three cars and a chopper.

00:29:03.204 --> 00:29:04.296
Two miles up Edgemont Road.

00:29:04.338 --> 00:29:05.635
This is it, men.

00:29:13.147 --> 00:29:15.377
Get into position
behind the house.

00:29:15.416 --> 00:29:17.907
Butchie and me'll
take these two.

00:29:17.985 --> 00:29:18.917
Another clip?

00:29:18.986 --> 00:29:19.918
Yeah.

00:29:19.987 --> 00:29:20.976
There.

00:29:24.091 --> 00:29:25.786
Looks like
your friends out there

00:29:25.826 --> 00:29:27.225
still believe in violence.

00:29:27.261 --> 00:29:29.024
Too bad for you.

00:29:36.135 --> 00:29:37.261
Let's recap.

00:29:37.303 --> 00:29:43.435
UFO in orbit, laser pistols,
people... vanishing.

00:29:43.476 --> 00:29:45.876
I've seen every episode
of Mission: Impossible.

00:29:45.912 --> 00:29:47.243
You're not secret agents.

00:29:47.280 --> 00:29:49.510
I told you,
I can't talk about it.

00:29:49.549 --> 00:29:52.040
Well, you can't keep a girl
from hypothesizing.

00:29:52.084 --> 00:29:53.574
I'm a scientist.

00:29:53.619 --> 00:29:55.883
I'm thinking...

00:29:55.922 --> 00:29:58.390
I'm thinking
alternate dimension.

00:29:58.424 --> 00:29:59.584
I'm thinking...

00:29:59.625 --> 00:30:01.115
close encounter.

00:30:01.160 --> 00:30:02.559
Whatever.

00:30:02.595 --> 00:30:05.758
Talk about a motley crew.

00:30:05.798 --> 00:30:08.323
We have the Doctor...

00:30:08.367 --> 00:30:11.302
a guy with the worst,
worst taste in clothing

00:30:11.337 --> 00:30:13.237
I've ever seen.

00:30:13.272 --> 00:30:16.070
Tuvok... what a freakasaurus.

00:30:16.108 --> 00:30:18.440
Has the guy ever
cracked a smile?

00:30:18.477 --> 00:30:21.344
Not that I can recall.

00:30:21.380 --> 00:30:26.215
And you... Tom Paris.

00:30:26.252 --> 00:30:28.117
Hmm, sexy...

00:30:28.154 --> 00:30:30.782
in a Howdy Doody sort of way.

00:30:30.823 --> 00:30:32.654
Pretty goofy,

00:30:32.692 --> 00:30:34.785
although sometimes
I think you're...

00:30:34.827 --> 00:30:36.590
the smartest man I've ever met.

00:30:36.629 --> 00:30:40.588
All this running around you do...
your mission...

00:30:40.633 --> 00:30:43.158
you're so dedicated, you know?

00:30:43.202 --> 00:30:46.535
Like you care about something
more than just your own...

00:30:46.572 --> 00:30:47.834
little life.

00:30:50.343 --> 00:30:51.708
Is that so unusual?

00:30:53.679 --> 00:30:55.442
Yeah.

00:30:59.018 --> 00:31:00.918
Whoa. I missed the turn.

00:31:10.062 --> 00:31:13.657
SATCOM 47 activating.

00:31:17.670 --> 00:31:20.298
Engage Starling location sweep.

00:31:20.339 --> 00:31:22.000
Sweep underway.

00:31:37.657 --> 00:31:38.783
We're in Arizona.

00:31:38.824 --> 00:31:41.554
Chakotay and Torres are 30
kilometers northeast of Phoenix.

00:31:41.594 --> 00:31:42.993
Good. Get to them
as soon as you can.

00:31:43.029 --> 00:31:43.996
Captain.

00:31:44.030 --> 00:31:45.520
There's a transport in progress.

00:31:46.399 --> 00:31:47.388
What?

00:31:49.435 --> 00:31:50.493
Starling's gone.

00:31:50.536 --> 00:31:51.867
He's beamed to the surface.

00:31:51.904 --> 00:31:54.236
He's got some kind
of satellite in orbit.

00:31:54.273 --> 00:31:55.240
It sent a transporter signal

00:31:55.274 --> 00:31:56.741
through our shields
like they weren't there.

00:31:56.776 --> 00:31:57.868
Where's Starling now?

00:31:57.910 --> 00:31:59.309
Tracking the signal.

00:31:59.345 --> 00:32:01.711
He's back
at the Chronowerx building.

00:32:09.655 --> 00:32:12.283
Mr. Dunbar, good work.

00:32:12.324 --> 00:32:14.224
I think it's time
to get out of here.

00:32:29.175 --> 00:32:30.938
I guess this is good-bye.

00:32:30.976 --> 00:32:32.910
I guess it is.

00:32:32.945 --> 00:32:37.814
Listen... are you
busy tomorrow night?

00:32:37.850 --> 00:32:39.283
'Cause, um...

00:32:39.318 --> 00:32:43.254
you know,
we should hang together.

00:32:43.289 --> 00:32:45.382
I can't.

00:32:45.424 --> 00:32:47.824
Oh. Well,
what about this weekend?

00:32:47.860 --> 00:32:50.454
Um...

00:32:50.496 --> 00:32:52.293
You're married.

00:32:52.331 --> 00:32:54.196
Absolutely not.

00:32:54.233 --> 00:32:56.758
Just...

00:32:56.802 --> 00:32:58.667
very busy.

00:32:58.704 --> 00:33:01.832
Oh... yeah, you got
to get back to Mars, right?

00:33:01.874 --> 00:33:03.171
Hmm... Saturn.

00:33:04.643 --> 00:33:05.735
That's perfect.

00:33:05.778 --> 00:33:08.246
I told you
I always loved Saturn.

00:33:08.280 --> 00:33:10.874
So, give me your phone number.

00:33:10.916 --> 00:33:11.940
Rain...

00:33:15.588 --> 00:33:17.818
Tachyon emissions.

00:33:21.794 --> 00:33:23.523
They're moving the timeship.

00:33:23.562 --> 00:33:25.928
Timeship?
What are you talking about?

00:33:25.965 --> 00:33:30.459
You wouldn't mind hanging
with me for a while longer, huh?

00:33:34.140 --> 00:33:35.664
We want the aircraft

00:33:35.708 --> 00:33:37.767
and the occupants
from the aircraft.

00:33:37.810 --> 00:33:39.778
Get off my land!

00:33:39.812 --> 00:33:41.746
What are they going
to do when they find

00:33:41.781 --> 00:33:42.907
a half-Klingon in here?

00:33:42.948 --> 00:33:43.915
Who the hell are you two?!

00:33:43.949 --> 00:33:45.917
Please stand aside, Officer.

00:33:45.951 --> 00:33:47.145
I'm warning both of you...

00:33:49.889 --> 00:33:51.447
They've got lasers.

00:33:51.490 --> 00:33:53.685
A black man and some bald guy.

00:34:14.113 --> 00:34:16.604
God in heaven help us.

00:34:16.649 --> 00:34:19.413
Divine intervention is...
unlikely.

00:34:32.698 --> 00:34:34.063
Tuvok's at the shuttle.

00:34:34.099 --> 00:34:35.430
He's starting repairs.

00:34:35.467 --> 00:34:36.434
Doctor, how?

00:34:36.468 --> 00:34:37.935
It's a long story, Commander.

00:34:37.970 --> 00:34:41.607
Suffice it to say,
I'm making a house call.

00:34:54.319 --> 00:34:55.752
It's Paris again, Captain.

00:34:55.787 --> 00:34:56.754
On audio.

00:34:56.788 --> 00:34:57.948
Status report, Tom.

00:34:57.990 --> 00:34:59.787
We just turned off
the main highway

00:34:59.825 --> 00:35:01.087
onto a desert road.

00:35:01.126 --> 00:35:03.287
Hi. This is Rain Robinson.

00:35:03.328 --> 00:35:04.886
You don't know me,
but the point is,

00:35:04.930 --> 00:35:06.795
there is zero traffic
on this road.

00:35:06.832 --> 00:35:08.197
They're going to know
we're following them.

00:35:08.233 --> 00:35:09.666
Thank you, Miss Robinson.

00:35:09.701 --> 00:35:11.032
I'll keep that in mind.

00:35:11.069 --> 00:35:12.434
Tom, we've scanned the area.

00:35:12.471 --> 00:35:14.462
There appears to be
a small landing field

00:35:14.506 --> 00:35:16.167
about ten kilometers
ahead of you.

00:35:16.208 --> 00:35:17.607
It could be his launch site.

00:35:17.643 --> 00:35:18.610
Stay on him.

00:35:18.644 --> 00:35:20.202
Our weapons are still off-line

00:35:20.245 --> 00:35:22.372
and Torres hasn't finished
repairing the shuttle.

00:35:22.414 --> 00:35:24.314
It might all be up to you.

00:35:24.349 --> 00:35:26.510
I'll do my best.
Paris out.

00:35:39.398 --> 00:35:40.023
Look out!

00:35:50.409 --> 00:35:51.569
Get in behind him.

00:35:51.610 --> 00:35:52.599
What?

00:35:52.644 --> 00:35:54.236
Right off his bumper.

00:36:06.224 --> 00:36:07.486
A little closer.

00:36:07.526 --> 00:36:08.322
Forget it.

00:36:08.360 --> 00:36:09.918
One more meter!

00:36:09.995 --> 00:36:10.927
Just shoot!

00:36:25.744 --> 00:36:27.336
It's flooded.
Give it a second.

00:36:27.379 --> 00:36:28.903
Well, do you think we got him?

00:36:28.947 --> 00:36:30.437
I think so.

00:36:42.461 --> 00:36:43.860
Come on!

00:36:45.764 --> 00:36:46.389
Jump!

00:36:59.411 --> 00:37:01.072
Chakotay to Paris.

00:37:01.113 --> 00:37:02.205
What's your status?

00:37:03.348 --> 00:37:05.009
We're fine.

00:37:05.050 --> 00:37:06.711
Good shooting.

00:37:08.153 --> 00:37:11.213
Wasn't there supposed to be
a timeship in that truck?

00:37:14.659 --> 00:37:16.217
I'm scanning the debris.

00:37:16.261 --> 00:37:17.523
It was a temporal transponder

00:37:17.562 --> 00:37:19.291
set to give off
tachyon signals.

00:37:19.331 --> 00:37:20.525
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:37:20.565 --> 00:37:22.726
The timeship's not here,
Captain.

00:37:22.768 --> 00:37:23.928
It was a ruse.

00:37:23.969 --> 00:37:26.096
Starling's going to launch
from a different site.

00:37:31.243 --> 00:37:32.642
Activate hyper-impulse.

00:37:32.677 --> 00:37:35.510
Hyper-impulse drive engaged.

00:37:35.547 --> 00:37:37.845
Let's do it.

00:37:37.883 --> 00:37:39.544
Command confirmed.

00:37:52.230 --> 00:37:54.425
The timeship is entering
the upper ionosphere.

00:37:54.466 --> 00:37:55.694
Track his course.

00:37:55.734 --> 00:37:57.964
Janeway to Shuttlecraft.
Return to Voyager immediately.

00:37:58.003 --> 00:37:59.231
Acknowledged, Captain.

00:37:59.271 --> 00:38:01.262
Phasers are still off-line.

00:38:01.306 --> 00:38:04.002
I've armed the photon torpedoes,
but we still can't fire them.

00:38:04.042 --> 00:38:07.068
The launch activation sequencers
aren't responding.

00:38:07.112 --> 00:38:09.342
I think I can reroute fire
command through the helm.

00:38:09.381 --> 00:38:10.575
There's no time.

00:38:10.615 --> 00:38:12.549
Take the Bridge, Mr. Kim.

00:38:12.584 --> 00:38:13.608
Should be second nature

00:38:13.652 --> 00:38:15.279
- to you by now.
- Captain...

00:38:15.320 --> 00:38:17.754
Open the access portal
to Torpedo Bay 1.

00:38:17.789 --> 00:38:20.053
I'm going in there to
reconfigure for manual launch.

00:38:20.091 --> 00:38:22.252
Captain, with the activation
sequencers down,

00:38:22.294 --> 00:38:23.761
you'd have to launch
from inside the tube.

00:38:23.795 --> 00:38:24.762
It's too dangerous.

00:38:24.796 --> 00:38:25.763
The plasma exhaust...

00:38:25.797 --> 00:38:26.786
You have your orders.

00:38:33.138 --> 00:38:35.231
I've got the transporters
back on line.

00:38:35.273 --> 00:38:37.241
Mr. Paris, stand by.

00:38:37.275 --> 00:38:38.333
We're bringing you aboard.

00:38:38.376 --> 00:38:39.775
Acknowledged.

00:38:42.881 --> 00:38:44.678
Your spaceship's waiting.

00:38:48.086 --> 00:38:50.316
I've never met anyone
quite like you...

00:38:52.324 --> 00:38:54.417
and I don't think I ever will.

00:38:55.694 --> 00:38:57.958
Same here.

00:39:01.099 --> 00:39:02.896
Say hi to Saturn for me.

00:39:05.503 --> 00:39:06.663
I will.

00:39:31.863 --> 00:39:33.455
Initiate temporal inversion.

00:39:33.497 --> 00:39:35.397
Initiating.

00:39:40.738 --> 00:39:42.330
Bridge to Janeway.

00:39:42.373 --> 00:39:43.431
The shuttle's back on board.

00:39:43.474 --> 00:39:44.771
Good. I'm nearly there.

00:39:44.809 --> 00:39:47.209
Captain, the timeship
has jumped to warp 1.

00:39:47.245 --> 00:39:49.975
Go to warp.
We can't lose him now.

00:39:53.985 --> 00:39:55.145
Welcome to the Bridge, Doctor.

00:39:55.186 --> 00:39:56.710
Thank you.
It's a pleasure to be here.

00:39:56.754 --> 00:39:58.221
Status?

00:39:58.256 --> 00:40:00.349
The Captain's in Torpedo Tube 1.

00:40:00.391 --> 00:40:02.052
She's preparing
for a manual launch.

00:40:02.093 --> 00:40:03.253
Doctor, get down there.

00:40:05.296 --> 00:40:07.958
How exactly do I get
to Torpedo Tube 1?

00:40:08.032 --> 00:40:09.260
Ensign Kaplan, go with him.

00:40:09.300 --> 00:40:10.426
Aye, sir.

00:40:14.572 --> 00:40:17.837
The timeship is powering
its temporal field generator.

00:40:17.875 --> 00:40:20.275
Starling will be able to open
a rift within seconds.

00:40:20.311 --> 00:40:22.745
Commander, the field he's
creating... it's unstable.

00:40:22.780 --> 00:40:24.372
If he enters
the rift like this,

00:40:24.415 --> 00:40:26.679
that timeship will create
a temporal explosion.

00:40:26.717 --> 00:40:29.743
Events are occurring just
as Captain Braxton predicted.

00:40:29.787 --> 00:40:32.620
The disaster may well
be inevitable.

00:40:32.657 --> 00:40:33.988
Fate, Tuvok?

00:40:34.058 --> 00:40:35.423
I won't accept that.

00:40:35.459 --> 00:40:36.756
Close to within ten kilometers.

00:40:36.794 --> 00:40:38.227
We'll ram him if we have to.

00:40:38.262 --> 00:40:39.251
Aye, sir.

00:40:41.032 --> 00:40:43.830
Temporal core has reached
cascade potential.

00:40:45.536 --> 00:40:50.235
Penetration point
at 96 mark 047.

00:40:56.981 --> 00:40:57.948
Janeway to Bridge.

00:40:57.982 --> 00:40:59.244
I've reconfigured
for manual launch.

00:40:59.283 --> 00:41:00.409
Arm the torpedo.

00:41:00.451 --> 00:41:01.850
Torpedo armed.

00:41:03.587 --> 00:41:05.578
Lock on target.

00:41:05.623 --> 00:41:06.681
Locked on.

00:41:06.724 --> 00:41:07.748
Hail Starling.

00:41:07.792 --> 00:41:08.850
On screen.

00:41:08.893 --> 00:41:10.952
This is Voyager.

00:41:10.995 --> 00:41:12.860
Pull away from the rift.

00:41:12.897 --> 00:41:13.955
Or what?

00:41:13.998 --> 00:41:16.330
Your weapons are down, friend.

00:41:16.367 --> 00:41:18.995
See you... sometime.

00:41:21.138 --> 00:41:22.332
Chakotay to Janeway.

00:41:22.373 --> 00:41:24.534
Captain,
we have no other choice.

00:41:24.575 --> 00:41:26.099
He's entering the rift.

00:41:27.345 --> 00:41:28.334
Fire!

00:41:36.354 --> 00:41:37.582
Uh-oh.

00:41:43.427 --> 00:41:46.692
Captain, I insist
you come to Sick Bay.

00:41:46.731 --> 00:41:49.495
There'll be plenty
of time for that, Doctor.

00:41:53.604 --> 00:41:54.866
The Bridge is yours, Captain.

00:41:54.905 --> 00:41:57.135
Is there a chance in hell
we can reopen that rift?

00:41:57.174 --> 00:41:58.436
Captain...

00:41:58.476 --> 00:42:00.501
the rift is opening.

00:42:00.544 --> 00:42:02.535
There's something coming out.

00:42:02.580 --> 00:42:03.877
It's the timeship.

00:42:03.914 --> 00:42:04.881
Let's see it.

00:42:04.915 --> 00:42:05.779
We are being hailed.

00:42:05.816 --> 00:42:06.805
On screen.

00:42:08.386 --> 00:42:10.479
Captain Braxton?

00:42:10.521 --> 00:42:11.749
Do you know me?

00:42:11.789 --> 00:42:13.780
Yes, unfortunately.

00:42:13.824 --> 00:42:16.349
You tried to destroy our ship
in the 24th century,

00:42:16.394 --> 00:42:18.419
and the next time we saw you,

00:42:18.462 --> 00:42:21.124
you were an old man,
homeless in 1996.

00:42:21.165 --> 00:42:22.962
I never experienced
that time-line.

00:42:23.067 --> 00:42:24.557
Then what are you doing here?

00:42:24.602 --> 00:42:26.570
In my century,
we can scan time...

00:42:26.604 --> 00:42:28.799
much as you use sensors
to scan space.

00:42:28.839 --> 00:42:31.501
The Temporal Integrity
Commission detected your vessel

00:42:31.542 --> 00:42:33.271
over 20th century Earth.

00:42:33.310 --> 00:42:34.709
I was sent
to correct that anomaly.

00:42:34.745 --> 00:42:36.645
Prepare to follow me back
into the rift.

00:42:36.680 --> 00:42:39.240
I'm returning you
to your own time

00:42:39.283 --> 00:42:41.513
to your previous coordinates
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:42:41.552 --> 00:42:43.611
Captain...

00:42:43.654 --> 00:42:46.179
we've been trying
to get home to Earth

00:42:46.223 --> 00:42:47.622
for the last two years.

00:42:47.658 --> 00:42:49.649
Can you return us
to our century,

00:42:49.693 --> 00:42:51.991
but keep us here
in the Alpha Quadrant?

00:42:52.096 --> 00:42:53.757
I'm sorry.

00:42:53.798 --> 00:42:55.322
Temporal Prime Directive.

00:42:55.366 --> 00:42:57.664
I'm afraid you're on your own.
Braxton out.

00:43:03.174 --> 00:43:05.369
The timeship
is reentering the rift.

00:43:11.549 --> 00:43:13.574
Mr. Paris...

00:43:16.954 --> 00:43:18.546
follow him in.

00:43:20.758 --> 00:43:21.918
Aye, Captain.

00:43:29.333 --> 00:43:33.565
Captain's Log, Stardate 50312.5.

00:43:33.604 --> 00:43:35.401
We are again
in the Delta Quadrant

00:43:35.439 --> 00:43:36.838
at the exact time and place

00:43:36.874 --> 00:43:38.865
we first encountered
the timeship.

00:43:38.909 --> 00:43:40.740
I've resumed a course for Earth

00:43:40.778 --> 00:43:44.179
and I've ordered the crew
to the Mess Hall for a toast.

00:43:45.683 --> 00:43:46.650
Cheers.

00:43:46.684 --> 00:43:47.651
New beginnings.

00:43:47.685 --> 00:43:48.652
Here, here.

00:43:48.686 --> 00:43:49.653
To the future.

00:43:49.687 --> 00:43:50.711
Here, here.

00:43:50.754 --> 00:43:53.552
How long will you be
out and about, Doctor?

00:43:53.591 --> 00:43:55.786
If you're referring
to my newfound mobility,

00:43:55.826 --> 00:43:57.259
that is entirely up to me.

00:43:57.294 --> 00:43:58.591
I'm still trying to figure out

00:43:58.629 --> 00:44:01.462
exactly how the Doctor's
autonomous emitter works,

00:44:01.499 --> 00:44:03.330
but it looks like
downloading him back

00:44:03.367 --> 00:44:04.459
into the ship's computer

00:44:04.502 --> 00:44:06.197
isn't going to be
much of a problem.

00:44:06.237 --> 00:44:08.228
Apparently,
the reverse is also true.

00:44:08.272 --> 00:44:10.502
I will be able to make use
of the emitter as casually

00:44:10.541 --> 00:44:12.475
as you might slip
on a pair of shoes.

00:44:12.510 --> 00:44:14.944
It's a little more
involved than that.

00:44:15.045 --> 00:44:18.208
You know, Kes,
now that I'll be to-and-fro,

00:44:18.249 --> 00:44:20.513
your responsibilities
in Sick Bay will increase.

00:44:20.551 --> 00:44:23.179
I'm up to the challenge,
Doctor, but what about you?

00:44:23.220 --> 00:44:25.552
There's going to be more to
your life now than Sick Bay.

00:44:25.589 --> 00:44:27.056
Nothing I can't handle.

00:44:27.091 --> 00:44:30.083
You know, Captain, I've always
wanted a little more privacy.

00:44:30.127 --> 00:44:32.322
Perhaps under the circumstances,
my own quarters.

00:44:32.363 --> 00:44:34.228
One step at a time, Doctor.

00:44:37.201 --> 00:44:38.065
You should have seen it

00:44:38.102 --> 00:44:39.831
when the parking
enforcement officer

00:44:39.870 --> 00:44:40.928
came over to the van.

00:44:40.971 --> 00:44:43.201
Tuvok tried to use
pure Vulcan logic

00:44:43.240 --> 00:44:45.208
to talk her out of
giving us a citation.

00:44:45.242 --> 00:44:46.209
Did it work?

00:44:46.243 --> 00:44:47.210
Of course not.

00:44:47.244 --> 00:44:49.804
Given Mr. Paris'
alleged familiarity

00:44:49.847 --> 00:44:51.075
with 20th century America,

00:44:51.115 --> 00:44:53.174
it is a wonder we survived
the experience at all.

00:44:55.119 --> 00:44:57.110
Tuvok...

00:44:57.154 --> 00:44:58.587
has anyone ever told you,

00:44:58.622 --> 00:45:01.318
you're a real freakasaurus?
